id: pm-beads-cjey
title: Release coverage gate is below 100 percent and omits executable tooling
description: "The baseline release gate passes because package thresholds are lines 91 branches 77 and functions 93 over index.ts only. Actual measured coverage is 93.40 percent lines 80.33 percent branches and 95.28 percent functions; no independent statements metric is reported, and executable TypeScript gates plus the JavaScript merge-driver helper are outside the measured production set. This is separate from the canonical CLI migration."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: coverage,quality-gate,release-blocker,tdd,typescript
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:20:42.513Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T10:37:12.254Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T08:05:06.925Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T08:05:06.925Z"
claim_principal: ox-alpha
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "Define the complete production source inventory including executable tooling; eliminate or migrate the remaining JavaScript helper to erasable TypeScript; establish independently measured 100 percent coverage of lines branches and functions (V8 reports statements as lines, so the lines threshold IS the statements metric on this runtime and no separate statements check exists) without ignore directives or artificial tests; add mutation or adversarial checks that prove the gate fails on an unexecuted source and each threshold regression; keep tests fast nonduplicative and behavior-focused; include the exact gate in release check and CI; document literal scope and results"
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: pm-beads main d4f36b5 baseline release check with 115 tests
repro_steps: "Run NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check and inspect the coverage table and package.json coverageGate sources thresholds; inspect scripts/prepare-merge-driver.mjs."
resolution: exact-coverage-achieved
expected_result: Release and CI fail unless every executable production source reaches genuine independent 100/100/100/100 coverage and all production code is TypeScript or Rust.
actual_result: "Baseline observation (pre-fix, recorded at issue creation): the gate then passed at 93.40 percent lines 80.33 percent branches and 95.28 percent functions over index.ts only with thresholds 91/77/93, reported no statements metric, and excluded executable tooling. Final result: exact independent 100/100/100 coverage (lines/branches/functions) over index.ts plus all executable tooling, enforced with sources ['.','scripts'] and ignore [] — see close_reason."
component: release quality and source policy
customer_impact: A green release check currently permits uncovered production behavior and cannot substantiate the mandatory four-dimensional coverage claim.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T05:09:19.723Z",ox-alpha,"Branch fix/exact-coverage-gate created off baf512f. Inventory: index.ts, scripts/coverage-gate.ts, scripts/docstring-gate.ts, scripts/prepare-merge-driver.mjs (to migrate to erasable TS). Working region by region through the uncovered error/refusal paths."
tests[1]{command,scope}:
  "npm run release:check",project
docs[4]{path,scope}:
  scripts/coverage-gate.ts,project
  scripts/docstring-gate.ts,project
  scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts,project
  test/gates-scripts.test.ts,project
close_reason: "Exact independent 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines achieved and enforced. Scope: index.ts plus all executable tooling (scripts/coverage-gate.ts, scripts/docstring-gate.ts, scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts) = 4 source files reported by the gate; V8 reports statements as lines so the lines threshold IS the statements metric on this runtime (documented in CoverageThresholds). Changes: (1) coverage-gate.ts restructured into pure runGate/evaluateRun/collectReportedFiles exports behind an isMainInvocation guard (docstring-gate contract), so the gate is itself measured by its own suite and drivable against fixture repos; root argument now required at invocation (fail-closed). (2) prepare-merge-driver.mjs migrated to erasable TypeScript with injectable platform/PATH/exec; .mjs deleted; npm prepare updated. (3) coverageGate strengthened to sources ['.','scripts'] with thresholds exactly 100/100/100 and ignore []. (4) Adversarial/mutation checks added: fixture-repo tests prove the gate fails naming an unexecuted source, fails a threshold regression, rejects every ignore-entry escape (not-under-sources, unverifiable compiler, missing emit, runtime-emitting), refuses stale/missing lcov reports, strips runner-context env so nested measurement cannot silently skip the report, and proves the shipped script fails closed when run as main without a root. (5) 287 tests total across 8 files; all failure/recovery paths of the importer/exporter/diff/validate driven black-box through a scripted real pm executable (test/fixtures/stub-pm.ts). Gates: npm run release:check exit 0 (typecheck+build+docstring+coverage+audit+pack+deterministic changelog); identical npm run coverage step present in ci.yml so CI enforces the exact gate."
body: ""
